  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 314 AM EDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nFriday through Tuesday...\n\nMoving into the late week, the upper flow across the eastern CONUS \nwill remain blocking with a strong ridge building from the lower MS \nValley northward into the western Great Lakes while a deep upper \nlevel low will be found over the NE US.  We should see much drier \nair working into the region with some building heights coming in \nfrom the west.  With partly to mostly sunny skies expected, we'll \nsee temperatures moderate a bit.  The coolest readings will be in \nthe northeast/Bluegrass region with lower 70s, but mid-upper 70s \nwill be found in the I-65 corridor and back into western KY. Clear \nskies and light winds will allow good radiational cooling to occur \nFriday night and Saturday morning with lows dropping into the lower-\nmid 40s over the Bluegrass with mid-upper 40s in the I-65 corridor \nand western KY.\n\nRidging will continue to build across the region for Saturday \nresulting in a beautiful fall day with a decent amount of sunshine \nand highs topping out in the 73-78 degree range.  Lows Saturday \nnight will drop back into the upper 40s/around 50 in the Bluegrass \nwith lower 50s across the I-65 corridor and back toward the I-165 \narea.  Highs on Sunday will be similar to Saturday with perhaps a \nbit of high cloudiness moving into far western KY.  Will go with \nhighs in the 74-79 degree range here with overnight lows in the \nupper 40s/lower 50s.\n\nFor Monday/Tuesday, flow pattern will change slightly across the \nCONUS with a deep upper and surface low bringing very showery/windy \nconditions to the NE US while a ridge will be found across the \ncentral US.  The Ohio Valley will remain in a northerly flow aloft \non Monday transitioning to more of a westerly flow by Tuesday. \nTemperatures should continue to slowly moderate on Monday with highs \nin the upper 70s east of I-65, and west of I-65, we'll see highs \nmainly in the lower 80s.  Further moderation is expected by Tuesday \nwith highs warming into the lower 80s in the east with mid-upper 80s \nin the west.",
